# Verification & Completion

## Verification Before Completion

Before completing any task:

- Run linting (`next lint` or project-specific lint command).
- Run typechecking (`tsc --noEmit` or project-specific typecheck).
- Run relevant tests.
- Verify imports resolve correctly.
- Verify no hydration/runtime errors exist.
- Verify no TypeScript errors exist.
- Verify no console warnings were introduced.
- Confirm implementation matches existing architectural patterns.
- If using Playwright E2E, run the affected spec and inspect trace on failure.
- If using Next.js DevTools MCP, confirm no compilation or runtime errors are reported.

---

## Failure Recovery

When verification fails:
1. Inspect logs and runtime errors.
2. Identify root cause before modifying additional code.
3. Avoid stacking speculative fixes.
4. Revert ineffective changes quickly.
5. Prefer one verified fix at a time.

---

## Completion Criteria

A task is complete only when:

- TypeScript passes.
- Lint passes.
- Relevant tests pass.
- The feature works end-to-end.
- No placeholder code remains.
- No obvious regressions were introduced.
- The implementation follows existing project conventions.
